                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Suppose, for example, that policymakers are interested in how a policy that simultaneously increases ungendered employment and work segregation equality affects the gender equality level in the country, as measured by the GEI. Imposing high segregation equality together with high employment levels aims to ensure that, as employment rises, jobs across different business areas are distributed equally between women and men. To simulate such a policy, we instantiate Work segregation equality and Employment rate to their maximum level. Moreover, given the high level of geographical heterogeneity that characterizes Italian regions, policy makers may also be interested in how the policy would affect different areas. In order to accomplish this goal, the node Geographical area is instantiated to two exemplifications: Italian macro-regions, namely North-East and South, and the results are compared. The obtained distributions of the GEI and its domains are reported in Table 4, together with the relative baselines.",
